# Task 144-014: Docker HB Deploy Wire (Sprint 139 Fix Canlı)

## Baseline
- `spawn-backend-docker.ts` uses plain `writeFileSync` for HB writes (line 213, 356)
- `atomicWriteFileSync` exists in `worker-lifecycle.ts` but is NOT wired into Docker backend
- Docker backend script template already has `fsync_file` POSIX trap (Sprint 139)
- heartbeat-daemon.ts uses async `writeFile` which is fine for daemon context
- Existing tests in `tests/e2e/docker-hb-shutdown.test.ts` (21 tests)

## Changes

### 1. spawn-backend-docker.ts — Wire atomicWriteFileSync
- Import `atomicWriteFileSync` from `../agents/worker-lifecycle.js`
- Replace `writeFileSync(hbPath, ...)` with `atomicWriteFileSync(hbPath, ...)` at:
  - Line 213: Initial HB write after container start
  - Line 356: monitorContainer HB update on exit
- Add host-side fsync for HB in `verifyResultAfterStop` (also fsync HB file)

### 2. heartbeat-daemon.ts — Minor hardening
- Already async, no atomicWrite needed
- Add `atomicWriteFileAsync` pattern for HB file consistency if needed
- Actually: heartbeat-daemon.ts is NOT about Docker HB — it's about HEARTBEAT.md tasks
- Minimal change: ensure daemon PID file write is atomic

### 3. tests/docker/docker-hb.test.ts — 10 E2E tests
- Test atomicWriteFileSync HB wire in Docker backend
- Test HB gap <5s (heartbeat interval verification)
- Test SIGTERM grace period 15s
- Test fsync_file script template
- Test EXIT/TERM traps in script
- Test host-side post-stop verification
- Test reconciliation (exitCode != 0 but result DONE)
- Test HB sequence increment
- Test container script heartbeat loop interval
- Test fallback result write
